  "system_note": "Claim MR_SNF_02 — Revenue line 1 billed 0192 (rehabilitation therapy), units=10, DOS range 2026-06-02 to 2026-06-15. Review of the record shows: (1) an interdisciplinary plan of care documenting skilled PT/OT planned 5-7x/week (INTERDISCIPLINARY PLAN OF CARE - SNF STAY, pp. 10-11); (2) a PT evaluation documenting a qualifying prior inpatient hospitalization discharged 06/02/2026 (Physical Therapy, pp. 18-20); and (3) therapy progress notes on ten dates within the billed range documenting high-minute skilled therapy sessions (example: PT progress note documents “Total minutes this session: 90 minutes (6 billable units) | Revenue Code: 0421”) that align with the 0192 rehabilitation per-diem level. The payer-specific guideline for Aetna Medicare Advantage was not available in the dataset; the payer-agnostic reference guide confirms the concept of a “skilled need” and maps revenue code 0192 to rehabilitation therapy (Policy Documents/SNF/Reference Materials/SNF Level of Care - Definitions and Reference Guide.docx, positions 6 and 8). Per-diem-level determination fields returned null for individual dates; the retrieval tool’s note explains that a null level_determination_statement commonly means the facility had no exception to document because the billed level's minute threshold was met that day (get_per_diem_level_notes result note). Taken together — documented plan of care calling for frequent skilled PT/OT, a qualifying hospital discharge the day of SNF admission, and repeated PT/OT progress notes showing 90 PT minutes + 60 OT minutes on the ten billed dates — the medical record supports the billed 0192 per-diem level for the ten days billed. Citations: INTERDISCIPLINARY PLAN OF CARE - SNF STAY, pp. 10-11; Physical Therapy evaluation, pp. 18-20; PT progress notes (example p.25); Policy Documents/SNF/Reference Materials/SNF Level of Care - Definitions and Reference Guide.docx, positions 6 and 8; get_per_diem_level_notes result note.",
